# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore for the Course 1 project repository
#
# Copy this to the repo root as `.gitignore` BEFORE the first `git add`.
# Order matters: a file ignored after it has already been committed stays in
# history, and on a public repo that history is published.
#
# Two jobs here:
#   1. keep credentials and local state out of the repo entirely
#   2. keep the submission to the files the rubric asks for
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- credentials and local environment ------------------------------------
# The first block is the one that matters. Everything here is either a
# credential or a file that conventionally holds one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials
config.ini
.netrc
.pypirc
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519
.aws/
.aws-sam/

# ---- the virtual environment ----------------------------------------------
# Each coursework project gets its own venv, destroyed at teardown. It never
# belongs in the repo: it is large, platform-specific, and can contain
# absolute paths from this machine.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.Python

# ---- infrastructure state --------------------------------------------------
# Terraform state is plaintext and routinely contains secrets pulled from
# resource attributes. This stays listed even while the project uses no IaC,
# so that adding Terraform later cannot accidentally publish state.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
crash.log

# ---- ML artefacts ----------------------------------------------------------
# Large binaries do not belong in git. The model the project serves should be
# fetched from the registry or the Hub at build time, which is also what makes
# the deployment traceable to a version.
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.h5
*.safetensors
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
.dvc/cache/
.dvc/tmp/
data/raw/
data/interim/
*.parquet
*.db
*.sqlite3

# ---- local tooling and scratch --------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---- submission hygiene ----------------------------------------------------
# Graded submissions carry only what the instructions and rubric require, so
# preparation instruments and working notes stay out of the repo. These are
# run from a sibling directory, never committed.
submission-prep/
scratch/
notes-local/

# ---- additions specific to this project -----------------------------------
# The deepchecks language-model cache. lid.176.bin is ~126 MB and is fetched
# from dl.fbaipublicfiles.com on first use; it is a cache, not a deliverable.
.deepchecks_models/

# Kept from the starter's own .gitignore.
/models

# DVC stage outputs are tracked by DVC, not git. `dvc repro` writes a
# data/.gitignore listing them, which IS committed — that file is how a
# cloner knows which paths DVC owns.
